  "reviewer": "Codex implementation review; not independent security certification",
  "scope_review": "Pure recordless contract and queue only; no native TLS Engine is exported. Complete pure-module import closure, independent tests, negative compiler fixtures, separate host/provider consumer, owning build and exact compiler identity are bound. A provider fixture is explicitly synthetic. Native Debug ran 13 external tests plus a cached two-test internal executable; the direct counter-debug run reran those two tests. ReleaseSafe ran all 15 tests. Seven cross builds are compile-only. The relocated SDK-free consumer is supplemental evidence in t01-extra-runs/runs.json and relocation.json; its cwd is outside the repository and it is not normalized into a false local run. Contract input configuration uses explicit host-selected values; no ambient or native defaults are consulted. Borrowed Plan verification detects drift, not authorization or certificate-file identity. Trusted consumer actions are synchronous, serialized and must be retry-safe on failure. Wider Engine/provider/platform/resource/interop requirements remain separate planned packages.",
